 "notes": [
  "Block positions for 700/800/900/1500/1800/2100/2600/3600 MHz are taken from BNetzA's 'Drahtloser Netzzugang 700 MHz bis 3,8 GHz' chart (Stand 23.08.2021), updated for the March 2025 extension decision (BK1-22/001).",
  "BNetzA decision of 24 Mar 2025: paired 800/1800/2600 MHz rights expiring 31 Dec 2025 extended to 31 Dec 2030; Vodafone's 1760–1785/1855–1880 MHz extended from 2033 to 2036; unpaired 2.6 GHz (2570–2620 MHz) and unpaired 2 GHz not extended. A larger award of 800/1800/2600 plus the 2033-expiring 700/900/1500/1800 rights is planned for use after 2030.",
  "Conditions of the extension: incumbents must negotiate cooperative sharing of ≥2×5 MHz sub-1 GHz spectrum with 1&1 in its build-out areas; Telefónica must continue leasing 2×10 MHz at 2.6 GHz to 1&1 (new lease 2026–2030 signed Nov 2025). Negotiations on sub-1 GHz failed by 31 Dec 2025; BNetzA consulted on ordering sharing (deadline 18 Mar 2026). The outcome after that is not reflected here.",
  "Local licences: 3700–3800 MHz (campus networks, >120 holders) and 24.25–27.5 GHz (local assignments on application) are not national and are not attributed to any operator."
 ],
 "missing": [
  "1&1's 2.6 GHz lease position (2660–2670/2540–2550 MHz) is from davwheat/EARFCN only, not a regulator source.",
  "Outcome of BNetzA's 2026 proceeding on ordering sub-1 GHz sharing for 1&1 (consultation closed 18 Mar 2026) could not be confirmed.",
  "450 MHz (450connect, utilities) not compiled (optional group).",
  "2300 MHz status is from background knowledge (no MFCN assignment), not source-verified.",
  "EARFCN/NR-ARFCN values are from davwheat and not re-verified; the O2 B1 EARFCN was dropped because O2's B1 block shrank to 2×10 MHz in 2026."
 ],
 "changes": [
  "2100: O2 reduced from 2×20 to 2×10 MHz (2130–2140/1940–1950); 1&1 added at 2140–2150/1950–1960 MHz from 1 Jan 2026 (2019 auction).",
  "2600 FDD: fixed reversed O2 uplink ([2560,2550] → 2550–2570); noted 1&1 block is a lease from O2; expiry now 2030.",
  "2600 TDD (B38): changed to not-assigned — rights expired 31 Dec 2025 and were not extended.",
  "3.7–3.8 GHz: removed the pseudo-operator 'Regional licenses'; now shown as grey unassigned local-licence block (not national).",
  "1800: split blocks by expiry (2030/2033/2036) per BNetzA; 800 expiry now 2030.",
  "Operators renamed to current brands/legal entities (O2 Telefónica, 1&1 Mobilfunk GmbH); colours adjusted so O2 and 1&1 are distinguishable.",
  "Added not-assigned entries for 600, 850, 1700, 1900, 2000tdd, 2300, 4900, 26g, 40g, 47g; 1400 range narrowed to the assigned core band.",
  "Positions upgraded to 'verified' where they match BNetzA's assignment chart."
 ],
